    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0386" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/220</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-19T18:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 19, 1916, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 20, 8.10 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5343. Your circular December 16, 5 p. m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d139-f1"/> Lord
                        Robert Cecil has just informed me that the British
                    Government will decline the German proposal to discuss peace because it contains
                    no concrete terms with which such a discussion might begin and for other
                    reasons; and that the Prime Minister will set forth the Government’s position in
                    full in the speech which he is now delivering in the House of Commons.</p>
                <p>I will telegraph the text of what the Prime Minister says at the earliest hour
                    possible.</p>
                <p>Lord Robert informed me that the British
                    Government had requested the French Government to draw up the reply of the
                    Allies to the note of the Central powers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
